    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high offensive output today, anchored by the elite tier production of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Young (xERA 4.78) and significant park factors, resulting in a robust 19% boost from the opposing pitcher's profile. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a top-tier asset; his 16% park factor bump and a strong platoon advantage against Yesavage make him an essential engine for our daily totals. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.88) also rounds out our core, leveraging a 14% platoon edge against King to solidify his status as a must-start at 2B.\n\nThe decision to keep **Coby Mayo** (49.79) on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same park factor that elevated **Gunnar Henderson**, his projected efficiency dipped due to a negative platoon split against Yesavage, forcing him below our internal threshold for active utility slots. Conversely, we are navigating risks with our outfielders: **Kyle Tucker** (52.36) and **Andy Pages** (48.06) are facing the formidable Luzardo (xERA 3.28). While both possess the talent to outperform these projections, their scores are suppressed by Luzardo\u2019s elite skill profile, particularly for **Kyle Tucker**, whose base projection suffers an 18% hit based on the matchup. \n\nWe are closely monitoring the bottom of our lineup, where **Nasim Nunez** (49.36) remains a marginal play. Despite his utility, he faces an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher in King, which introduces a -4% penalty to his score due to the high probability of suppressed stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical category for our 5x5 strategy. **Jackson Merrill** (47.18) shares similar risk, as his efficiency is mitigated by a 13% penalty against Griffin\u2019s platoon profile and a negative adjustment for facing a catcher with a quick pop time. Managers should remain alert for late-breaking lineup changes, as any shift from these projected orders could necessitate a re-evaluation of our efficiency scores before first pitch.",
